# API walkthrough - VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
#
# The two passwords come from docs/.env (gitignored) - create it with two lines,
#     ADMIN_PWD=...
#     SALES_PWD=...
# then click "Send Request" above each block in order. The login block captures the
# tokens; every later request reads them.
# Access tokens live 5 minutes by default (JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_LIFETIME_MINUTES in the
# repo-root .env; set to 180 for this walkthrough). Re-send block 1.1 when you see 401s.
#
# Companion to docs/TESTING_GUIDE.md, which says what to expect from each request.

@host = http://localhost:8000
@admin = Administrator
@admin_pwd = {{$dotenv ADMIN_PWD}}
@sales = ada@example.com
@sales_pwd = {{$dotenv SALES_PWD}}

# =========================================================================================
# STEP 1 - auth and envelopes
# =========================================================================================

### 1.1 Login as Administrator -> 200, {"message": {"access", "refresh", "user", ...}}
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/method/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"usr": "{{admin}}", "pwd": "{{admin_pwd}}"}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.message.access}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.$.message.refresh}}

### 1.2 Who am I -> 200, {"message": "Administrator"}
GET {{host}}/api/method/frappe.auth.get_logged_user
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.3 Same call with no token -> 401, exc_type AuthenticationError
GET {{host}}/api/method/frappe.auth.get_logged_user

### 1.4 A method that does not exist -> 404, exc_type DoesNotExistError
GET {{host}}/api/method/crm.api.no_such_thing
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.5 Wrong password -> 401, "Invalid login credentials"
POST {{host}}/api/method/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"usr": "{{admin}}", "pwd": "definitely-wrong"}

### 1.6 Missing parameter -> 417, exc_type ValidationError, "Both usr and pwd are required"
POST {{host}}/api/method/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"usr": "{{admin}}"}

### 1.7 Refresh -> 200, a NEW access and refresh pair (the old refresh is now blacklisted)
# @name refreshed
POST {{host}}/api/method/token/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refresh": "{{refresh}}"}

### 1.8 Re-use the OLD refresh token -> 401, "Token is blacklisted"
POST {{host}}/api/method/token/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refresh": "{{refresh}}"}

### 1.9 Logout with the new refresh token -> 200, {"message": {"message": "Logged Out"}}
POST {{host}}/api/method/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"refresh": "{{refreshed.response.body.$.message.refresh}}"}

### 1.10 Log in again so the rest of the file has a live token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/method/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"usr": "{{admin}}", "pwd": "{{admin_pwd}}"}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.message.access}}

# =========================================================================================
# STEP 2 - one doctype through all five CRUD routes: CRM Organization
# =========================================================================================

### 2.1 Create -> 201, name == organization_name (field: naming, verbatim)
POST {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organization_name": "Acme Test Co", "website": "https://acme.test", "no_of_employees": "11-50"}

### 2.2 Create the same name again -> 409, exc_type DuplicateEntryError
POST {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organization_name": "Acme Test Co"}

### 2.3 Read one -> 200; note owner / modified_by / creation / modified came from BaseDocument
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization/Acme%20Test%20Co
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.4 List, default 20 rows, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.5 List with a field selection and a filter -> 200, one row, three columns
# The like-pattern is %acme% but a bare % is illegal in a URL, so it is written %25acme%25.
# The server decodes it back before the filter runs.
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization?fields=["name","website","modified"]&filters=[["website","like","%25acme%25"]]
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.6 `like` is case-insensitive on purpose (Postgres would not be) -> same row as 2.5
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization?fields=["name"]&filters=[["website","like","%25ACME%25"]]
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.7 `in`, dict-form filters, ordering, paging -> 200, ONE row (Acme)
# Two names match, but limit_page_length=1 asks for one row and "Acme" sorts before
# "Globex". Change limit_start to 1 to get the second page, which is Globex.
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization?fields=["name"]&filters={"name":["in",["Acme Test Co","Globex"]]}&order_by=name asc&limit_page_length=2&limit_start=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.8 Unknown field in fields= -> 417 (unknown names raise, they are not dropped)
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization?fields=["name","no_such_field"]
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.9 Relation traversal is refused -> 417
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization?fields=["owner__password"]
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.10 Update -> 200; modified changes, creation does not
PUT {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization/Acme%20Test%20Co
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"website": "https://acme.examples", "annual_revenue": 1250000}

### 2.11 A name with a slash is legal and addressable
POST {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organization_name": "R/GA"}

### 2.12 ...and reachable at a path-style URL -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization/R/GA
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.13a Delete R/GA -> 200, {"data": null}
DELETE {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization/R/GA
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.13b Delete Acme Test Co -> 200, {"data": null}
DELETE {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization/Acme%20Test%20Co
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.14 Read it back -> 404, exc_type DoesNotExistError
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization/Acme%20Test%20Co
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.15 A doctype that is not routable answers exactly like one that does not exist -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/resource/ToDo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# =========================================================================================
# STEP 3 - CRM Lead, then the method endpoints its screen uses
# =========================================================================================

### 3.1 Create a lead -> 201, name CRM-LEAD-2026-000NN (naming series), status auto-set to "New"
# lead_owner is the ACCESS column. Leave it out and a Sales User cannot see their own lead.
# @name lead
POST {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"first_name": "Walkthrough", "last_name": "Lead", "email": "walk@example.test", "organization": "Acme Test Co", "lead_owner": "{{admin}}"}

###
@lead_name = {{lead.response.body.$.data.name}}

### 3.2 Read it -> lead_name was composed by the model ("Walkthrough Lead"), status is "New"
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead/{{lead_name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.3 The list screen's real engine: get_data -> data + columns + rows + views in one payload
POST {{host}}/api/method/crm.api.doc.get_data
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"doctype": "CRM Lead", "filters": {}, "order_by": "modified desc", "page_length": 5, "view": {"view_type": "list"}}

### 3.4 `@me` resolves to the caller -> only leads whose lead_owner is you
POST {{host}}/api/method/crm.api.doc.get_data
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"doctype": "CRM Lead", "filters": {"lead_owner": "@me"}, "page_length": 5, "view": {"view_type": "list"}}

### 3.5 Assign it to a colleague -> writes a ToDo row, refreshes _assign
POST {{host}}/api/method/frappe.desk.form.assign_to.add
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"doctype": "CRM Lead", "name": "{{lead_name}}", "assign_to": ["{{sales}}"]}

### 3.6 _assign now lists ada -> one row, two columns
# The detail route (/<DocType>/<name>) always returns the whole document and ignores
# `fields`, matching Frappe. Field selection is a LIST-route feature, so this reads the
# one lead through the list route with a name filter.
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead?fields=["name","_assign"]&filters=[["name","=","{{lead_name}}"]]
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.7 Comment on it
POST {{host}}/api/method/crm.api.comment.add_comment
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference_doctype": "CRM Lead", "reference_name": "{{lead_name}}", "content": "<p>thank you CRM</p>"}

### 3.8 The timeline -> assignment, comment, and a "created" entry, newest first
POST {{host}}/api/method/crm.api.activities.get_activities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "{{lead_name}}"}

### 3.9 frappe.client.set_value is CRUD wearing a method name -> same effect as PUT
POST {{host}}/api/method/frappe.client.set_value
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"doctype": "CRM Lead", "name": "{{lead_name}}", "fieldname": "job_title", "value": "CTO"}

### 3.10 Status change -> also writes a CRM Status Change Log child row
PUT {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead/{{lead_name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "Contacted"}

### 3.11 Deals: list the newest two
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Deal?fields=["name","deal_owner","status","deal_value"]&limit_page_length=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.12 One deal in full, child tables inline (contacts, products)
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Deal/CRM-DEAL-2026-00101
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.13 Clean up the walkthrough lead
DELETE {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead/{{lead_name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# =========================================================================================
# STEP 4 - the same records as a Sales User
# =========================================================================================

### 4.1 Login as ada (Sales User)
# @name sales_login
POST {{host}}/api/method/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"usr": "{{sales}}", "pwd": "{{sales_pwd}}"}

###
@sales_token = {{sales_login.response.body.$.message.access}}

### 4.2 Her lead list -> only leads she owns or is assigned to (compare the count with 3.3)
POST {{host}}/api/method/crm.api.doc.get_data
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"doctype": "CRM Lead", "filters": {}, "page_length": 50, "view": {"view_type": "list"}}

### 4.3 A deal that is not hers -> 403, exc_type PermissionError (404 would mean it does not exist)
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Deal/CRM-DEAL-2026-00101
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}

### 4.4 Organizations have no row rule -> she sees all of them
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Organization?fields=["name"]
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}

### 4.5 A lead she creates without lead_owner vanishes for her -> 201, then 4.6 is empty
# @name orphan
POST {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"first_name": "Orphan", "last_name": "Lead", "email": "orphan@example.test"}

###
@orphan_name = {{orphan.response.body.$.data.name}}

### 4.6 -> 403: she created it and cannot read it back. This is upstream's rule, not a bug.
GET {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead/{{orphan_name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}

### 4.7 Administrator can, and cleans it up
DELETE {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Lead/{{orphan_name}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.8 She may not rewrite the org chart -> 403 (the tree is an input to the permission engine)
POST {{host}}/api/resource/CRM%20Sales%20Hierarchy
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"user": "{{sales}}"}

### 4.9 She may read her own User row but not change her roles -> groups is never on the wire
GET {{host}}/api/resource/User/{{sales}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}

### 4.10 Filtering on a hidden field is refused rather than answered -> 400, "Invalid Filter"
GET {{host}}/api/resource/User?filters=[["groups","like","%25Manager%25"]]
Authorization: Bearer {{sales_token}}
